WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:06.720
Over this weekend, we surpassed a&nbsp;
major covid vaccination milestone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:15.440
and we came very close to surpassing another. On&nbsp;
Saturday, the US injected two point nine million&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:23.120
vaccines into people's arms, almost half a million&nbsp;
more than the previous single day record of about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:31.120
two point four million vaccines in a day. And&nbsp;
we are just shy of three million vaccines a day.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:36.480
That is a real possibility. In the three days&nbsp;
this past weekend, Friday, Saturday, Sunday,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:43.440
more than seven point seven million vaccines&nbsp;
were injected in just three days. These are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:47.600
the types of numbers that will turn the&nbsp;
pandemic around if they can be sustained.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:52.480
Look at how quickly this has ramped&nbsp;
up. When Donald Trump left office,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.040 --> 00:01:01.600
the seven day average of vaccinations was 890000&nbsp;
a day, thanks to Joe Biden working with Pfizer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:06.560
and Moderna to ramp up supply to states and&nbsp;
getting the vaccine to states. Importantly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:11.440
because we had this situation under Trump where&nbsp;
Pfizer and Moderna were reporting deliveries,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:17.040
and yet hospitals and clinics were saying we don't&nbsp;
have the vaccines. So that has been improved. We&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:21.520
now have the addition of a third vaccine. We&nbsp;
may have a fourth vaccine. We are now averaging&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:26.320
two point one six million doses per day. Over&nbsp;
the last week. We have a new high water mark of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:32.480
two point nine million vaccines in a single day.&nbsp;
Right now, by percentage, the leading states on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:38.320
vaccination are New Mexico, Alaska, Connecticut,&nbsp;
the Dakotas, Rhode Island and Massachusetts.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:45.280
States doing the worst on vaccination percentage&nbsp;
wise are Georgia, Washington, D.C., which isn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:52.720
a state, Alabama, Texas, Utah and Tennessee. I&nbsp;
believe that in the next week, possibly Saturday,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:58.000
that seems to be the big vaccination day. Every&nbsp;
week we will get to three million vaccines in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:03.920
single day. And if you can make that study, you&nbsp;
are dramatically improving the timeline on herd&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:08.880
immunity compared to just doing a million vaccines&nbsp;
that you are. You are moving it up, in fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:17.440
by two thirds. The math of this is that if we can&nbsp;
accelerate to about three million doses per day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:23.360
we are looking at maybe three months until we&nbsp;
start getting into the range of what we would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:28.720
consider to be herd immunity. Could be could be&nbsp;
three. Could be four, could be two and a half.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:33.120
You know, if we get to four million doses a day,&nbsp;
we could really get even closer. It's not worth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:38.320
calculating it with too much precision. There's no&nbsp;
sense in saying May 10th will be the day, does it?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:43.280
You know that things change and shift. But when&nbsp;
you think about three and a half million a day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:49.200
that's two hundred and ten million doses in&nbsp;
60 days. If you assume 80 percent of those&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:55.280
are the two shot regimen and the rest are the one&nbsp;
shot, you're maybe looking at fully vaccinating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.280 --> 00:03:00.160
one hundred and twenty five million people in&nbsp;
the next two months. Thirty million are already&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:06.080
vaccinated. And then that means that like maybe&nbsp;
one more month, you know, 90 days from now, we are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:11.520
starting to get into the range. Of herd immunity&nbsp;
now there's tons of work to be done, we're racing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:16.480
against variants against which the vaccines are&nbsp;
not quite as effective in terms of preventing&nbsp;&nbsp;

